/* ****************************************************************************
 * __ABI__PASS_STACK__ (CDECL) ARGUMENT ACCESS
 *
 * THE OFFSETS ARE FRAME POINTER RELATIVE. YOUR SECTION MUST EXECUTE THE
 * STANDARD PROLOGUE BEFORE USING ANY MOV_<REG>_ARGn / MOV_ARGn_<REG>:
 *
 *   32-BIT: PUSH_EBP + MOV_EBP_ESP -> ARG1 = [EBP + 8], ARGn = [EBP + 4 + 4n]
 *   16-BIT: PUSH_BP  + MOV_BP_SP   -> ARG1 = [BP + 4],  ARGn = [BP + 2 + 2n]
 *           (NEAR CALLS; A FAR CALL ADDS 2 TO EVERY OFFSET)
 *
 * MOV_<REG>_ARGn LOADS ARGUMENT n INTO <REG>.
 * MOV_ARGn_<REG> STORES <REG> INTO ARGUMENT n.
 * WIDER REGISTER NAMES (RAX / EAX) ARE ROUTED TO THE WIDEST REGISTER THAT
 * EXISTS IN THE CURRENT MODE.
 **************************************************************************** */

